      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG4:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Jael, Heber’s wife, took a tent peg, and took a hammer in her hand, and went softly to him, and struck the pin into his temples, and it pierced through into the ground, for he was in a deep sleep; so he fainted and died."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG5:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Jael shall be blessed above women, the wife of Heber the Kenite; blessed shall she be above women in the tent."
